<title>BELGIUM: European Commission rejects Clabecq plan - radio.</title>
<headline>European Commission rejects Clabecq plan - radio.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has rejected a rescue plan for Belgian steel firm Forges de Clabecq, Belgian radio BRTN said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It gave no details.  </p>
<p>Belgian news agency Belga said the Commission had ruled the 1.5 billion franc plan broke European Union rules on aid for the steel industry. It would demand the company pay back 700 million francs in advances already received within two months.</p>
<p>The Commission noted that the company was only receiving regional government aid without calls on private shareholders. The company was being aided at a time when, technically, it was already bankrupt, Belga said quoting Commission sources.</p>
<p>The Commission had strong doubts about the viability of the company, even if large amounts of cash were invested, in view of the overcapacity in its market.</p>
